# Allow-list dockerignore: the build context is the repository root (see
# build/docker-compose.yml build.context), and this repo also holds several
# multi-GB per-pathogen data directories that must never enter that context
# or the image. Everything is excluded by default; only the paths the
# Dockerfile actually copies (build/, executables/, tests/, external/) are
# allowed back in. Adding a new top-level directory to the repo does NOT
# expose it to the build unless it is explicitly un-ignored below.
#
# Negation order matters: a directory has to be un-ignored before its
# contents can be, and once a directory is excluded, patterns can't reach
# inside it again - so each allowed path needs its own explicit line, not
# just a trailing /**.

*

!build/
!build/**

!executables/
!executables/**

!tests/
!tests/**

!external/
!external/**

# Keep caches and checkpoints out even from allowed directories.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
